6:8: warning: An `echo -e` relies on a bash builtin, and the POSIX `echo` prints the flag as text. (SC3037)
     6 |    echo -e escaped
       |         ^~
note: Use `printf` under a `sh` shebang.
7:8: warning: An `echo -n` relies on a bash builtin, and the POSIX `echo` prints the flag as text. (SC3037)
     7 |    echo -n nonewline
       |         ^~
note: Use `printf` under a `sh` shebang.
8:3: warning: The `declare` builtin is not in POSIX. (SC3044)
     8 |    declare -A assoc
       |    ^~~~~~~
note: Assign the variable plainly under a `sh` shebang, or switch the shebang to bash.
9:3: warning: The `typeset` builtin is not in POSIX. (SC3044)
     9 |    typeset scoped
       |    ^~~~~~~
note: Assign the variable plainly under a `sh` shebang, or switch the shebang to bash.
10:3: warning: The name `source` is the bash spelling of the POSIX `.` command. (SC3046)
    10 |    source library.sh
       |    ^~~~~~
note: Use `.` under a `sh` shebang.
13:7: warning: The `<(...)` process substitution is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh. (SC3001)
    13 |    cat <(echo substituted)
       |        ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use a named pipe or a temporary file under a `sh` shebang.
14:8: warning: The extended glob `!(excluded)` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh. (SC3002)
    14 |    echo !(excluded)
       |         ^~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use a `case` statement or a plain glob under a `sh` shebang.
15:8: warning: The `$'...'` quoting form is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh. (SC3003)
    15 |    echo $'a\tb'
       |         ^~~~~~~
note: Use `printf` to produce the escapes under a `sh` shebang.
16:8: warning: A `^` opens the bracket expression `[^a]tail`, and POSIX sh negates with `!`. (SC3026)
    16 |    echo [^a]tail
       |         ^~~~~~~~
note: Use `[! ...]` under a `sh` shebang.
17:3: warning: An `echo` of a command substitution prints what the command already prints. (SC2005)
    17 |    echo "$(<file)"
       |    ^~~~
note: Run the command on its own.
17:9: warning: The `$(<file)` form is a bash shorthand absent from POSIX sh. (SC3034)
    17 |    echo "$(<file)"
       |          ^~~~~~~~
note: Use `$(cat file)` under a `sh` shebang.
18:3: warning: An `echo` of a command substitution prints what the command already prints. (SC2005)
    18 |    echo "`<file`"
       |    ^~~~
note: Run the command on its own.
18:9: warning: The `` `<file` `` form is a bash shorthand absent from POSIX sh. (SC3035)
    18 |    echo "`<file`"
       |          ^~~~~~~
note: Use `$(cat file)` under a `sh` shebang.
19:9: warning: The indirect expansion of `!indirect` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh. (SC3053)
    19 |    echo "${!indirect}"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use `eval` or a `case` dispatch under a `sh` shebang.
20:9: warning: The array reference `array[0]` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh. (SC3054)
    20 |    echo "${array[0]}"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use the positional parameters under a `sh` shebang.
21:9: warning: The array key expansion of `!array[@]` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh. (SC3055)
    21 |    echo "${!array[@]}"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use the positional parameters under a `sh` shebang.
22:9: warning: The name prefix expansion of `!prefix*` is a bash extension absent from POSIX sh. (SC3056)
    22 |    echo "${!prefix*}"
